  "terminal_bridge": "A common runtime bug is the injection of dynamic metadata\u2014such as nonces, localized wall-clock timestamps (`Current Time: 21:07:59`), or randomized tool execution IDs\u2014at the head of the system prompt. Injecting a 10-token dynamic timestamp at index $\\mathbf{x}_1$ alters the integer sequence of the entire prompt, invalidating every downstream cache block in the Radix tree. The inference engine encounters a total cache miss at the root, evicts gigabytes of valid KV pages, and forces the accelerator to recompute the entire 40,000-token GEMM prefill from scratch. Disciplined context placement is not an aesthetic convention; it is the primary software control mechanism governing accelerator memory bus traffic and invocation cost.\n\nGiven these output properties and physical costs, how should engineers evaluate competing interface designs?"
